---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../lib/contact';
import { UNREVIEWED_PAGES } from '../lib/seo/unreviewed-pages';

const path = '/privacy';
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy" description="RayValue privacy policy: no cookies, privacy-friendly analytics, and what happens when you request installer quotes." path={path} noindex={UNREVIEWED_PAGES.has(path)}>
  <div class="page">
    <!-- TODO: owner legal review -->
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p>This is a plain description of what RayValue does with data today.</p>

    <h2>No cookies</h2>
    <p>RayValue does not set cookies and does not use advertising or cross-site tracking.</p>

    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      We use Vercel Web Analytics to count page views. It does not use cookies and reports only aggregated
      numbers, such as how many people viewed a page. We send page addresses without their query string, so the
      ZIP code and bill amount in a shared calculator link are not part of it.
    </p>

    <h2>The calculator</h2>
    <p>
      Your ZIP code, bill and other answers are used in your browser to run the estimate; we do not save them in a
      database unless you request installer quotes (see below). To look up how much sun your area gets, the rounded center point of your ZIP code (not your address)
      is sent to our server, which asks the PVWatts service run by the National Laboratory of the Rockies (formerly
      NREL). If you copy a link to your estimate, your answers are part of that link.
    </p>

    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>
      The site is hosted by Vercel. As with any website, the hosting provider processes request data such as IP
      addresses in order to serve pages and protect the site from abuse.
    </p>

    <h2>Quote requests</h2>
    <p>
      If you ask for installer quotes, we store what you enter in the quote form in our database (hosted by
      Supabase): your first name, email address, phone number, ZIP code and state, whether you own the home, and when
      you hope to go solar. When you send the form from your calculator results, we also store your calculator answers
      (utility, monthly bill, battery and shade) and the estimate you saw. We also store the exact consent wording you
      agreed to, when you agreed, the page you sent it from, and your browser&rsquo;s user-agent string.
    </p>
    <p>
      We use this to connect you with solar installers: we share it with up to 3 installers serving your area, as you
      agreed when you checked the consent box. They and RayValue may contact you about solar quotes. We do not share it
      with anyone else. We keep it until you ask us to delete it.
    </p>

    <h2>Rate change alerts</h2>
    <p>
      If you sign up for rate change alerts, we store your email address and your state in our database (hosted by
      Supabase), only to send you those alerts. We do not sell or share it.
    </p>

    <h2>Deleting or seeing your data</h2>
    <p>
      To ask us to delete your data, send you a copy, correct it, or stop sharing it, use our
      <a href="/privacy/request">privacy request form</a>. To stop calls, texts or emails from an installer, you can
      also tell that installer directly.
    </p>
    {CONTACT_EMAIL && (
      <p>You can also email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> from the address you gave us.</p>
    )}
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
